From f7ca00b47dfff3c19180591e3d7a8a6e9d71c47a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:53:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [GStreamer][MSE] Hold video decoding to the hardware-support
 setting

The media-content-types-requiring-hardware-support setting only shapes
what canPlayType(), MediaSource.isTypeSupported() and
requestMediaKeySystemAccess() report; whatever reaches the player is
decoded by the decoder playbin plugs, software included. A
SourceBuffer accepted because the CDM of the element's MediaKeys
decodes its video can still carry clear video. The MSE player now
fails a stream whose codec the setting reserves for hardware when a
software decoder receives it in the clear, with the codec matched by
its RFC 6381 and its WebM name. Encrypted input goes to a decoder
inside a CDM and stays allowed. Progressive playback is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
